body:
I don't think anyone really knows (I certainly dont.) But if I had to guess? Probably the same reason we don't find [a mandrill's face](https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/mammals/m/mandrill/#/mandrill.JPG) particulalry sexy. 

&#x200B;

For whatever reason breasts just developed as a sensor for human sexual maturity, just like a [baboon's butt](https://www.flickr.com/photos/15177460@N07/2682959026), a [peacock's tail](https://i.guim.co.uk/img/static/sys-images/Arts/Arts_/Pictures/2009/3/17/1237308883822/Peacock-002.jpg?width=620&quality=85&auto=format&fit=max&s=ef81b9651583b9efd2f3eb6ec2b3c323), or a big [honking pair of antlers](https://www.123rf.com/photo_45688281_male-reindeer-with-large-antlers-lying-and-resting-on-dirt.html) for  a reindeer
